  "$comment": "Every docs screenshot claims the dashboard shows certain words. This records the claim so tests/docs-screenshots.test.ts breaks when it stops being true. Prose drift is caught by the handbook corpus gate and check:cli; a screenshot of a renamed button stays wrong until a reader trips over it, and a confident wrong picture is trusted more than confident wrong prose. `sources` is load-bearing: a label must appear in the components that shot actually depicts, not anywhere under src/ui. A repo-wide substring sweep gated nothing - \"Block\" matched 86 files and \"Advise\" resolved against ConsultPage, so the policies shot passed while its caption contradicted the picture. Re-capture with demo/rec/docs-shots.mjs in the vibestrate-marketing repo, then update the labels here. The PNGs live in that repo because the docs site serves them; only the claim lives here, next to the source it is asserted against.",
